Choose a license before publishing.

For a specification document intended for community review and
eventual contribution to RISC-V International, **CC BY 4.0** is a
common choice for the text, and **Apache 2.0** is common for
reference RTL and software. Examples in the RISC-V ecosystem use
this pairing.

If you intend to keep this repository private until the CE Suite is
mature, you may wish to defer licensing entirely; in that case,
keep the repository private and the contents under default copyright.
